{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1772909437,"nonce":"REuje/r3MpGsh/Crf2/9aA6Ht+U=","message":"**Attempt-tracking — deep link from sessions task column**\n\nRoot cause identified: `findIssue()` calls `GET /api/issues/find/:id`. The API calls `issueScanner.findIssueAcrossRepos()` which searches the in-memory cache. After a daemon restart, the cache is empty — the async background scan hasn't completed. `apiGet` throws on 404, and the catch handler silently ignores it, so `selectedRepoId`/`selectedIssueId` are never set → 'select an issue to view details'.\n\nFix plan: in the deep-link useEffect catch block, call `onRescan()` to trigger a global scan, then retry `findIssue` once. Same pattern already used by the per-repo detail-fetch retry at line 268.","files":null}]}